                <pb facs="0240" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg150"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1740</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Moser</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-05-03T09:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 3, 1918, 9
                                a.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 5, 1.48 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Officially [announced] that Semenov force
                    has advanced to right bank of Onon River. As force nearly doubled by Cossacks,
                    volunteers <pb facs="0241" n="151" xml:id="pg151"/> will endeavor to cross Onon
                    and hold station of Olovyannaya ninety miles east of Karymskaya [omission] and
                    await there the receipt of further arms from Japan including armored [cars] now
                        <hi rendition="#italic">en route</hi>, also help, before undertaking to
                    advance beyond junction. Has now advanced appliances [headquarters] one mile
                    west of Manchuria [Station] and has requested Chinese Eastern Railway to assume
                    operation of [omission] lines as he advances. Is still receiving money and arms
                    from British and Japanese Governments. His advance has aroused enthusiasm and
                    force is said to have [increased] for past ten days.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Moser</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
